# ⭐ OPIc Sample Answer - Day35

Compared to the past, the way people communicate has changed dramatically.

In the past, people often made phone calls or sent letters when they wanted to communicate with someone who was far away.

These days, people mostly use smartphones and messaging apps.

The biggest change is that communication has become much faster and more convenient.

For example, I can send a message to my friends and get a response almost immediately.

I can also make video calls even when I'm in a different country.

As a result, it has become much easier to stay in touch with other people.

I think this change is very positive because we can communicate with people whenever and wherever we want.
